{"trial": "t01", "round": 1, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.332, "train_success_last10pct": 0.3174, "wall_s": 105.7, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.0005, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 2, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "Raising success_bonus from 1 to 5 makes exact matches much more valuable than partial cell credit, which should push the agent to finish builds precisely and call DONE at the right time. If dev success stays at about 0.33 or below, the reward is not limiting performance."}
{"trial": "t02", "round": 1, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.6602, "train_success_last10pct": 0.6542, "wall_s": 188.3, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 1.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "The agent underfits, so more learning per sample should help: 4 PPO epochs, lr 1e-3, and gamma 0.99 with lambda 0.95 so that credit for the end-of-episode success reaches early placements. If there is no gain, or training becomes unstable, sample efficiency is not the bottleneck."}
{"trial": "t03", "round": 1, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.9961, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9852, "wall_s": 423.0, "params": 128646, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 4, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "This combines the three changes above (depth 4 with layernorm, success_bonus 5, 4 epochs, lr 1e-3, gamma 0.99) to check whether their gains add up. It should still finish well under 600 s. If it does no better than the best single change, the changes interact or are redundant."}
{"trial": "t04", "round": 2, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.9961, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9856, "wall_s": 423.5, "params": 128646, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 4, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "This is an exact repeat of t03 with a new seed, run only to measure noise. If it lands below about 0.97, t03's 0.996 was partly seed luck, and the selection should favour more robust or cheaper variants."}
{"trial": "t05", "round": 2, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.7188, "train_success_last10pct": 0.7042, "wall_s": 233.6, "params": 128646, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 2, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 4, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "This is t03 with ppo_epochs cut from 4 to 2, which should take about 250 s instead of 423 s. If dev success stays at or above 0.98, the extra epochs are not needed, and this gives a much safer recipe to retrain. A clear drop means the extra sample reuse matters."}
{"trial": "t06", "round": 2, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.9961, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9829, "wall_s": 308.4, "params": 91590, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 3, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "This is t03 with depth 3 instead of 4, which cuts compute by about a quarter while keeping layernorm and the learning-intensity changes. A 3-layer field of view may already cover the 5x5 grid well enough. If dev success falls below 0.95, the fourth layer is needed."}
{"trial": "t07", "round": 2, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.4961, "train_success_last10pct": 0.4806, "wall_s": 424.8, "params": 128646, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 2, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 4, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "This is t03 with n_minibatches cut from 4 to 2, which halves the number of gradient steps per epoch while keeping 4 epochs and lowers per-step overhead, so it should run faster. If dev success stays at or above 0.98, it is a cheaper and robust alternative. A drop means the number of gradient updates drives the gain."}
{"trial": "t08", "round": 3, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.998, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9893, "wall_s": 305.0, "params": 91590, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 3, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "This is an exact repeat of t06 with a new seed, run to measure noise for the cheaper leader. If it lands below about 0.97, depth 3 is less robust than depth 4 and t03/t04 should be preferred."}
{"trial": "t09", "round": 3, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.7305, "train_success_last10pct": 0.7254, "wall_s": 170.8, "params": 91590, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 2, "n_minibatches": 8, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 3, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "This is t06 with 2 epochs and 8 minibatches. It keeps 16 gradient steps per rollout but processes half as much data, so it should take about 180 s. If dev success is at least 0.98, the number of updates, not the number of passes over the data, is what matters, and this gives a very safe recipe. A drop like t05's refutes that."}
{"trial": "t10", "round": 3, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.998, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9787, "wall_s": 309.1, "params": 91590, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 8, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 3, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "This is t06 with 8 minibatches, which doubles the gradient updates for roughly the same compute (about 330 s). It tests whether the 510/512 ceiling can be broken. Reaching 512/512 means the ceiling is not hard. Staying at exactly 0.9961 again strongly suggests 2 dev designs are unreachable or misjudged by the checker."}
{"trial": "t11", "round": 3, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.998, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9822, "wall_s": 190.4, "params": 54534, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "This uses depth 2 with layernorm, success_bonus 5 and the strong-learning settings (4 epochs, lr 1e-3, gamma 0.99), which should take about 200 s. t02 (depth 2, no norm, bonus 1) reached 0.66, so this isolates whether layernorm and the bonus can stand in for depth. A result below 0.95 means at least 3 layers are needed."}
{"trial": "t12", "round": 4, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.998, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9806, "wall_s": 190.7, "params": 54534, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "Exact repeat of t11 (depth 2, layernorm, about 190 s) with a new seed, run only to measure noise. If it lands at 0.99 or higher, the cheapest recipe is robust and a strong selection candidate. A result below 0.97 means depth 2 is seed-fragile and depth 3 should be preferred."}
{"trial": "t13", "round": 4, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.998, "train_success_last10pct": 0.986, "wall_s": 305.8, "params": 91590, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 8, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 3, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "Exact repeat of t10 (depth 3, 8 minibatches) with a new seed, run only to measure noise. Its doubled update count should keep it further from the update-count cliff seen in t07 and t09. A result at 0.99 or higher supports it as the robust pick; a drop below 0.97 refutes that."}
{"trial": "t14", "round": 4, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.9961, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9856, "wall_s": 306.4, "params": 91590, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 128, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 3, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "t08 with n_envs halved to 128. This doubles the number of rollouts and policy updates at the same sample cost, which should move the recipe further from the cliff. Expect about 0.998 at under 400 s. A drop below 0.99, or a timeout, means a smaller batch hurts stability."}
{"trial": "t15", "round": 4, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.9961, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9789, "wall_s": 191.6, "params": 54534, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 8, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "t11 (depth 2) with 8 minibatches. This doubles the gradient steps in a cheap network (about 200 s) and adds margin against the update-count cliff. A score at 0.996 or higher gives a fast, robust candidate; anything below t11 means more steps destabilise the shallow net."}
{"trial": "t16", "round": 5, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.9961, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9845, "wall_s": 312.8, "params": 91590, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 128, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 8, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 3, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "Depth 3 with n_envs 128 and 8 minibatches gives four times t08's gradient updates for the same samples and compute (about 310 s), so it should sit furthest from the update cliff. Expect 0.996 or higher. A drop below 0.99 would mean too many small-batch updates hurt stability."}
{"trial": "t17", "round": 5, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 1.0, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9853, "wall_s": 190.4, "params": 54534, "config": {"lr": 0.002, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.99, "gae_lambda": 0.95, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "layernorm", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "The cheap depth-2 recipe (t11/t12) with lr raised to 0.002 tests whether we have learning-rate margin on the high side (about 190 s). A score of 0.996 or higher means the recipe tolerates a stronger lr and is robust in both directions. A drop below 0.98 means lr 1e-3 sits near an upper stability limit, which argues for the deeper, lower-variance recipes."}
